Date: Sun, 17 Jan 93 12:39:50 EST
From: habs@panix.com (Harry Shapiro)
Subject: Self: Spped Reading

I friend of my father once hired a "famous" speed reading teacher
to teach the technique to his sons, staff and a few family friends 
(including myself). I was able to "achive" speeds of up to
2000 words per mintues in a very short time.

However, such techniques are not very useful. The most useful
part of the technique is using your fingers to help focus and
pace your eye movements as you "read" the page.

However, given a "paper" of high s/n like this list, a technical
manual or a cook book and such techniques generally fall flat.
(You can speed read "facts" only fluff.)

It is helpful though to speed read a book, and then re-read it
at a normal "pace."

Today I read about 200 to 400 wpm depending on the material.

/Harry

