Date: Sun, 17 Jan 93 14:40:08 EST
From: habs@panix.com (Harry Shapiro)
Subject: Meta: Metzger vs. Singh

I have been asked to by Mr. Singh to make a formal judgement against
Mr. Metzger.

This post is divided into three sections:
	Statement of Charges
	Discussion of Charges
	Punishment and Discussion of Punishment

* Statement of Charges *
Mr Singh found the following post by Mr. Metzger to violate
the list rules:

Paragraph 1
> Go and do what you want. However, given that you are a barely tolerated
> person on the list, don't expect any of us to pay you any attention or
> participate in any of your ventures. 

Paragraph 2
> In my opinion, you should just go off and use your advanced yogic techniques
> to produce duplicates of yourself that you may then converse with so that
> the rest of us need not be subjected to you discourse on the topic.

* Discussion of Charges *
I have examined the previous paragraphs and do not find that
paragraph 2 in any way violates list rules. However, I do feel
it would have been best if Mr. Metzger had sent paragraph directly
to Mr. Singh.

I have also examined paragraph 1.

Mr. Metzger makes two points to Mr. Singh:

	1 you are a barely tolerated person on the list

	2 don't expect any of us to pay you any attention

One way I read these comments is that they are both personal attacks on
Mr. Singh, and as such they are inflammatory. Such communication is in
violation of list rules.

Another way to read these comments is that they are simple statements
of fact or excepted theory, and as such, no matter how "inflammatory"
are welcome communication to the list. If these statements are based
upon fact, one would have expected, as is the common practice on the
list, that Mr. Metzger would have provided references to his source.
For example the results of a poll, or a restatement of previous posts,
etc. Of course, the lack of reference(s), doesn't directly imply that
Mr. Metzger's statements are not facts.

Over that past 3 weeks I have met with over 35 members of the list
at various extropian gatherings and I must say the topic of flying
yogis (A topic Mr. Singh has posted about) has come up. From
this limited and rather self-selected group I can draw the conclusion
that, in theory, Mr. Singh's post was not well tolerated. 

I can generally say, in theory, that Mr. Singh was not well respected
among those I spoke to. However, clearly judging by the responses to
many of his posts, many list members are or have "paid him attention."

Thus, I would say many while known and frequent posters to the list
would agree with Mr. Metzger's comments, the evidence of their
certitude is largely circumstantial. Lacking hard sources for Mr.
Metzger statements, I would say the information presented in them is
based more on heresay and personal informal observations then the
methods of science. Thus I do not except them as fact. Given the
reputation Mr. Singh has concerning his posts about "flying" I would
say that Mr. Metzger's comments are a reasonable theory about the
majority of the list members options of Mr. Singh.

Thus I find Mr. Metzger to be in technical violation of the
list rules and customary practices.

1) Not stating sources for his facts
2) Not differing between fact and theory
3) Making a general post to the list, when a personal reply
   to Mr. Singh would have been more effective.

I also find that Mr. Metzger's comments about list members'
"paying attention" to Mr. Singh to be neither true in fact
nor theory.

1) I find that Mr. Metzger has made an inflammatory statement,
   which is a clear violation of list rules.

* Punishment and Discussion of Punishment *
Mr. Metzger is a valued and long standing member of this list. He
is also the founding member of the list and a personal friend.

Never-the-less, he is not above the rule of law.

For his three technical violations of list law, and given
his lack of previous convictions, I give him a warning.

Mr. Metzger has previously been given two (of three) warnings by the
list adjudicator and one warning (previous) from me for making
inflammatory posts.  Since those warning were given Mr. Metzger has
made great efforts not to make such comments and I have viewed his
posts as model posts for this list. Clearly I would like that trend to
continue, but the time for warnings has past. I hope that the
following punishment, while limited in nature, will both help Mr.
Metzger to make no inflammatory posts in the future, while reaffirming
to Mr. Metzger his valued membership on this list.

I judge that Mr. Metzger should not make a post to this list from 11:59
PM on 1/17/93 to 11:59 PM on 1/18/93.

I judge that Mr. Metzger should consider reposting his excellent post
on list etiquette that he made to the Cryonics list to this list, either
prior to or after his posting "band."

I judge that Mr. Metzger can postpone, by indicating so in a post,
the posting band for a period of exactly 1 week, should he choice to
appeal this judgement - the postponement, being granted so that he
will not suffer should his appeal be granted and so that sufficient
time be given for his appeal to be made.

I judge that Mr. Singh, given the limited nature of my judgement
against Mr. Metzger be granted the right to appeal to the list
adjudicator (andreag@csmil.umich.edu) for a stiffer punishment.

I note to Mr. Metzger and Mr. Singh that upon appeal the list
adjudicator can confirm, reverse, amend, or completely alter this
judgement. The result could be a punishment weaker, stronger or
different than these judgements.

